        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[AI] fix(memory): use truncateUtf16Safe for dreaming snippet truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where dreaming snippet truncation in `memory-core` can produce invalid UTF-16 output. When a complex emoji or surrogate pair straddles the 280-character truncation boundary, `.slice(0, 280)` cuts between the high and low surrogate code units, producing a lone surrogate that can cause display corruption, JSON encoding failures, or database rejections downstream.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nReplace all 5 `.slice(0, N)` calls in `extensions/memory-core/src/dreaming-phases.ts` with `truncateUtf16Safe` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-core-host-engine-foundation` (the standard SDK facade, already used by `manager-search.ts` in the same extension). `truncateUtf16Safe` checks whether the cut position falls inside a surrogate pair (high surrogate `0xD800–0xDBFF` followed by low surrogate `0xDC00–0xDFFF`) and drops the orphaned high surrogate. The change is +6/-5 in a single file.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nNone for typical text content. For memory content that happens to contain an emoji or complex Unicode character at the truncation boundary, the dreaming snippet no longer includes a lone surrogate character, preventing potential downstream encoding issues.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n**Environment**: Linux x86_64, Node v24.13.1, OpenClaw 2026.6.11, commit `9ae8803b90`.\r\n\r\n### 1. Lone surrogate reproduction at the 280-char boundary\r\n\r\nBoth `DAILY_INGESTION_MAX_SNIPPET_CHARS` and `SESSION_INGESTION_MAX_SNIPPET_CHARS` are `280` (`dreaming-phases.ts:99,109`). With emoji at position 279–280:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ node --import tsx -e \"\r\nimport { truncateUtf16Safe } from '@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice';\r\nconst text = 'A'.repeat(279) + '😀';\r\nconsole.log('.slice(0, 280):     last code unit 0x' +\r\n  text.slice(0, 280).charCodeAt(279).toString(16) + ' (LONE HIGH SURROGATE)');\r\nconsole.log('truncateUtf16Safe:   ' +\r\n  truncateUtf16Safe(text, 280).length + ' code units (clean)');\r\n\"\r\n.slice(0, 280):     last code unit 0xD83D (LONE HIGH SURROGATE)\r\ntruncateUtf16Safe:   279 code units (clean)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 2. Real dreaming ingestion proof — emoji in daily notes + session corpus\r\n\r\nA full dreaming sweep was run against the patched branch with emoji-rich content at the truncation boundary:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-core/src/surrogate-proof.test.ts --run\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe test:\r\n\r\n1. Creates a workspace with a daily note containing emoji at the 280-char boundary\r\n2. Creates a session transcript with emoji in both near-boundary and overflow positions\r\n3. Runs `runDreamingSweepPhases` (the full dreaming ingestion pipeline)\r\n4. Performs code-unit-level verification that the daily markdown output, session corpus output, and all log messages contain zero lone surrogates\r\n\r\n### 3. Existing unit test coverage\r\n\r\n```console\r\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-core/src/dreaming-phases.test.ts --run\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  50 passed (50)\r\n\r\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/normalization-core/src/utf16-slice.test.ts --run\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  18 passed (18)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 4. Import boundary (fixes Codex review finding)\r\n\r\nImport path updated from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice` → `openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-core-host-engine-foundation`, matching the existing SDK facade used by `manager-search.ts` in the same extension.\r\n\r\n### What was NOT tested\r\n\r\nFull dreaming ingestion sweep with real memory files containing emoji at the truncation boundary from a live production workspace. Covered by: 50 dreaming-phase unit tests, 18 utf16-slice tests, plus the new surrogate-proof integration test.\r\n\r\n**Proof test file**: `extensions/memory-core/src/surrogate-proof.test.ts`\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/dreaming-emoji-safe-truncation",
